# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional: cloud sync for the PhD tracker at /phd-tracker
#
# Leave every line blank and the tracker stays browser-local, which is
# the default and needs no setup at all. Fill them in and the tracker
# gains Google sign-in plus one Firestore document per user, so the same
# bench opens on any device.
#
# Setup, once:
#   1. Create a Firebase project.
#   2. Authentication → Sign-in method → enable Google.
#   3. Authentication → Settings → Authorised domains → add
#      eswarmachara.github.io (and localhost for development).
#   4. Firestore Database → create, then publish these rules:
#
#        rules_version = '2';
#        service cloud.firestore {
#          match /databases/{database}/documents {
#            match /users/{userId}/{document=**} {
#              allow read, write: if request.auth != null
#                                 && request.auth.uid == userId;
#            }
#          }
#        }
#
#   5. Project settings → Your apps → Web → copy the config values below.
#   6. Add the same four as GitHub repository secrets so the deployed
#      build picks them up (see .github/workflows/deploy.yml).
#
# These values end up readable in the built page, as every Firebase web
# config does. That is expected: the rule in step 4 is what actually
# keeps the data private to your account.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=
